ase  but mutations in the virus are causing  concern  a variant that is more infectious and is  less  controlled by the vaccine will continue  to spread  more rapidly even when we've got  vaccine around but what this does mean  is that particularly for people who  haven't who  not able to be vaccinated or have  declined vaccine if you're vulnerable  you are going to be at more risk now  with these new variants circulating than  you would have been with the  the older variants  public health england says all the  vaccines should still prevent serious  illness and death  but moderna is developing a tweaked  version of its jab against the south  african variant as a precaution  in the meantime lockdown will slow the  spread of  all versions of the virus if people  stick to the rules  thomas more sky news invoking
 

